# Build context trim for `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .` (root context, whole reactor).
#
# docker/Dockerfile deliberately does `COPY . .` rather than listing modules, so adding a module
# stays free. This file is what makes that cheap: it drops everything the build does not need, and
# no stale output leaks in.

.git
.gitignore

# Maven / Quarkus build output — regenerated inside the build stage. Copying it in would risk a
# stale target/ shadowing what the stage compiles.
**/target
**/target-ide

# Local env / IDE cruft
.env
.idea
.vscode
.sdkmanrc

# Docs and the docker/ dir itself: nothing in the build reads them, and keeping them out means
# editing the Dockerfile or a README does not bust the `COPY . .` layer.
*.md
docker
